# svc-registered (the bag's REGISTER): the registered item on the idle
# field. Platinum uses Y for it (decomp FieldInput_Update: PAD_BUTTON_Y → registeredItem; Diamond and
# Pearl used Select). With nothing registered Y shows the key-item info; the Bicycle registered in the bag
# gets on and off; the Coin Case shows the coins (the message names the count).
party 0 platinum:SPECIES_TURTWIG 12
give item platinum:ITEM_BICYCLE 1
give item platinum:ITEM_COIN_CASE 1
set state coins 120
warp platinum:MAP_HEADER_ROUTE_201 115 853 right
until idle
# Nothing registered: the key-item info message, closed by A
+1 press y
+1 release y
until message
+0 assert message open
+0 assert text platinum:Bag_Text_KeyItemInfo 0
+0 assert state playerState "walk"
advance text
+0 assert message closed
# The bag: KEY ITEMS, the Bicycle, REGISTER (USE, REGISTER, CANCEL)
+1 press x
+1 release x
until app start-menu
+1 tap entry:1
+1 assert app bag
+1 tap pocket:7
+1 tap row:0
+1 tap menu:1
+1 assert state registeredItem "platinum:ITEM_BICYCLE"
+1 press b
+1 release b
+1 press b
+1 release b
until app none
# Y gets on the bike; two tiles east; Y gets off
+1 press y
+1 release y
until state playerState "cycle"
+0 screenshot cycling
+1 press right
until position 117 853
+0 release right
until idle
+1 press y
+1 release y
until state playerState "walk"
until idle
# The Coin Case: its message shows the coins
+1 press x
+1 release x
until app start-menu
+1 tap entry:1
+1 tap pocket:7
+1 tap row:1
+1 tap menu:1
+1 assert state registeredItem "platinum:ITEM_COIN_CASE"
+1 press b
+1 release b
+1 press b
+1 release b
until app none
+1 press y
+1 release y
until message
+0 assert message open
+0 assert text platinum:Bag_Text_CoinCaseMessage 0 0=120
+0 assert state playerState "walk"
+1 press b
+1 release b
until idle
